<title>POLAND: Espebepe up again on debt deal hopes.</title>
<headline>Espebepe up again on debt deal hopes.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish builder Espebepe SA surged 9.1 percent to 7.8 zlotys in moderate trade as the stock continued to vacillate before the ailing firm's creditors meet on March 14 to mull possible debt restructuring, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;It appears there will be more big movements before the creditors meet,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>The stock had risen 70 percent since mid-February before falling 26 percent over the last three sessions.</p>
<p>Espebepe has 80 million zlotys in debts.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
